    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3945" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλειπ-τήριον</span></b> , τό,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>place for anointing</i> in
			gymnasia, or in Roman Thermae, used also as <i>sudatory</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				101
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Ign.</u>
				13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(1).1390.108
			</span></i> (Andania, <span class="entity">i B. C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				2782.25
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Herod.Med.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				10.10.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>paint-brush</i> (<i><span class="en">
				Cypr.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πήριον</span> cod.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>unguent</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καμμάρω</span>
			.</div>
